.*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
.* XMLGENP - Generate XML download member - Help Text                *
.*                                                                   *
.* By   Craig Rutledge,  6/19/2001                                   *
.*                                                                   *
.*-------------------------------------------------------------------*
:PNLGRP.
.*
:HELP name='XMLGEN/ALL'.
:IMHELP name=XMLGEN.
:IMHELP name='XMLGEN/XMLSCRIPT'.
:IMHELP name='XMLGEN/SCRIPTSRCF'.
:IMHELP name='XMLGEN/SRCTOFILE'.
:IMHELP name='XMLGEN/XMLMBR'.
:IMHELP name='XMLGEN/ENCODING'.
:IMHELP name='XMLGEN/AUTHOR'.
:EHELP.
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* HELP TEXT FOR THE COMMAND
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP NAME='XMLGEN'.
Generate XML download mbrs (XMLGEN) - Help
:P.
This command generates a source file member
containing validated, well-formed XML text with all the information
required to recreate your source members/objects on another system.
.*
:P.
The driver is a 'script' member in source file QXMLGENS where you describe
the source members and object types you want to associate together with
a particular application build.
The script member for this utility XMLGEN is in source file QXMLGENS
for you to review.
:P.Three commands included in this utility are used to build the
information in the script file.
.*
:LINES.
xmlgenINC  specify whether to generate text for install pgm
xmlgenMBR  define attributes of source members and objects
xmlgenCMD  define commands to be executed at runtime.
xmlgenSQL  define SQL statements to be executed at runtime.
xmlgenCND  define conditions.
:ELINES.
.*
:P.The xmlgenINC command must appear first in your script source, but
xmlgenMBR, xmlgenCMD and xmlgenSQL can be mixed in any sequence after
that and may be used any number of times.   Installer program execution
follows the same sequence of events defined in the script.
.*
:P.The xmlgenSQL command must be specified regarding to the
SQL naming convention. The system naming convention can not
be used.
.*
:P.You can use the XMLGENCND command to ask the user for conditions
when the INSTALL program runs. Use the XCND() keyword to link a
XMLGENMBR, XMLGENCMD or XMLGENSQL command to a condition. You may use
conditions to compile language specific versions of a shipped utility.
:EHELP.
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* HELP TEXT FOR XMLKEY PARAMETER
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='XMLGEN/XMLSCRIPT'.
Script member name  - Help
:XH3.Script member name (XMLSCRIPT)
:P.
Specifies the member name of a script member in file QXMLGENS
that contains the source and object information for this app.
:P.
This is a required parameter.
:PARML.
:PT.member-name
:PD.Specify the script member name.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* HELP TEXT FOR SCRIPTSRCF
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='XMLGEN/SCRIPTSRCF'.
Script source file - Help
:XH3.Script source file (SCRIPTSRCF)
:P.Specifies the name of the source file where the script for this app
is stored.
.*
:PARML.
:PT.:PK def.QXMLGENS:EPK.
:PD.The default source file, QXMLGENS will be used.
.*
:PT.source-file-name
:PD.Enter the source file name for the script member.
.*
:PT.:PK def.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The system searches the library list to find the library where the
source file is located.
.*
:PT.library-name
:PD.Enter the name of the library where the source file is located.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
.*
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* HELP TEXT FOR SRCFILE
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='XMLGEN/SRCTOFILE'.
Source file - Help
:XH3.Source file (SRCTOFILE)
:P.Specifies the name of the source file where the XML member will be created.
.*
:PARML.
:PT.:PK def.QXML:EPK.
:PD.The default source file, QXML will be used.
.*
:PT.source-file-name
:PD.Enter the source file name for the XML member.
.*
:PT.:PK def.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The system searches the library list to find the library where the
source file is located.
.*
:PT.library-name
:PD.Enter the name of the library where the source file is located.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
.*
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* HELP TEXT FOR XMLMBR
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='XMLGEN/XMLMBR'.
XML output member name - Help
:XH3.XML output member name (XMLMBR)
:P.Specifies the name of the output XML member.
.*
:PARML.
:PT.:PK def.*SCRIPT:EPK.
:PD.The name of the XML output member is set to the name of the
input script member.
.*
:PT.member-name
:PD.Name of the XML output member.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
.*
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* HELP TEXT FOR ENCODING
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='XMLGEN/ENCODING'.
Encoding of XML file - Help
:XH3.Encoding of XML file (ENCODING)
:P.Specifies the encoding of the XML file.
.*
:PARML.
:PT.:PK def.ISO-8859-1:EPK.
:PD.ISO-8859-1 should be fine for German character sets.
.*
:PT.UTF-8
:PD.The default encoding is UTF-8. UTF-8 should be fine
for US character sets.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
.*
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* HELP TEXT FOR OWNER
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='XMLGEN/AUTHOR'.
Application author - Help
:XH3.Application author (AUTHOR)
:P.Specifies the author of the application.
:EHELP.
.*
:EPNLGRP.
